# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [Unreleased]

### Fixed
- **`allowed_mentions=discord.AllowedMentions.none()` safety net**: Added to every `ctx.send()` and `channel.send()` call across the entire codebase (100+ calls). Even if `@everyone`/`@here` text accidentally appears in message content, Discord will never render it as a ping.
- **`?hide` / `?unhide` no longer ping in `?help`**: Docstrings changed from `"@everyone"` to `"everyone"` so the help menu no longer triggers mass pings.
- **Logging user mentions fixed**: The logging formatter now resolves users via `guild.fetch_member()` instead of `bot.fetch_user()`, so log mentions render as proper Discord pings instead of raw `<@id>` text.
- **`?ls noroles` member cache**: The command now fetches all members from the API before scanning to ensure the member cache is fully populated.

### Changed
- **`?nuke` rewrite**: Completely rebuilt with a reaction-based flow (green tick / red cross), a detailed embed showing channel stats and destruction steps, a 30-second timeout, and a success embed with a nuclear bomb GIF in the recreated channel. Also adds security: protected channel names blocked, announcement channels blocked, bot permission pre-check, and audit logging.

### Added
- **`?sendwm`**: Debug command to send the welcome DM to a specified user or the command author (prefix only, no auth required).
- **Welcome DM with Components V2**: Completely redesigned welcome DM with clean layout, Quick Links section, and three action buttons (How to Verify, Website, GitHub). The How to Verify button sends an ephemeral guide explaining the Wick captcha and Rules Screening process.
- **Rules commands bypass authorization**: `?r1`–`?r13`, `?r34`, and `?tldr` can now be used by anyone via prefix, even without the authorized role.
- **Thread lock emoji**: `?lock` now prefixes thread names with a lock emoji (🔒) instead of `[Locked]` text.

### Added
- **`?ls channels ?v`**: Audit which roles/users can view a specific channel via permission overwrites.
- **`?ls noroles`**: List all members who have no roles (only @everyone).
- **`?permits`**: Prefix-only command to show all available permits with their permissions and user counts in a Components V2 container.
- **Authorized role gate**: Only users with `AUTHORISED_ROLE_ID` (or the bot owner) can use bot commands. Unauthorized prefix commands are silently ignored; slash commands show a "Not Permitted" Components V2 card.
- **Non-appealable mutes**: `/timeout appeal:False` (slash) or `?mute @user 10m reason ?a` (prefix) marks a timeout as non-appealable. The appeals system skips the DM for non-appealable mutes.
- **Warn logging**: Warnings are now logged to `LOG_CHANNEL_WARNINGS_ID` via the centralized logging system.
- **Custom Discord emojis**: Replaced Unicode emojis with `<:greentick:1529045309081256026>` and `<:redtick:1529045360742502481>` in all bot embed titles, messages, and text content.
- **R13 (Use Common Sense)**: Added new rule R13 to the rules system.
- **`AUTHORISED_ROLE_ID`**: New `.env` variable to control which role can use the bot.

### Changed
- **Permit system works everywhere**: All moderation commands (kick, ban, timeout, warn, lock, unlock, purge, clean, slowmode, nickname, softban, unban, untimeout) now respect the custom permit system, not just native Discord permissions.
- **Components V2 moderation cards**: All moderation confirmations (kick, ban, softban, timeout, untimeout, warn, unwarn, lock, unlock, slowmode, nickname) now render as clean Components V2 containers with accent colors and no emojis.
- **Specific error messages**: Every error message now names the exact permission needed, tells the user to ask an admin, and explains where to fix it.
- **Server rules updated**: R1-R12 updated with new wording (R2 dating warning, R7 drugs/weed, R8 AI content policy, R9 English requirement, R10 streaming rules, R11 alt accounts/tags/pronouns, R12 ban appeal link). R34 removed.

### Removed
- **APPEAL_SUBMITTED log**: Removed the noisy "User submitted a timeout appeal" embed from the appeals log channel.

### Fixed
- **Tempban persistence**:
    - Tempbans used to be scheduled with an in-memory `asyncio.sleep` task, so any bot restart converted them into permanent bans. Tempbans are now persisted to the `tempbans` table in the main database and re-scheduled (or executed immediately if already expired) when the bot comes back online.
- **Appeals System**:
    - Timeout appeal notifications (including the `@here` staff alert) could be sent to arbitrary channels because the review channel was resolved by channel-name matching and fell back to the guild's first text channel (a public channel). Appeal content now only ever goes to the configured appeals channel.
- **Lint errors**: Fixed all ruff-detected issues across 13 source files (unused imports, bare excepts, one-liner statements, unused variables).

### Changed
- **Appeals System**:
    - `APPEALS_LOG_CHANNEL_IDS` now defaults to a single appeals channel and the new `APPEALS_LOG_CHANNEL_ID` config is the single source of truth for appeal destinations.
    - All `APPEAL_*` logging events (`APPEAL_SUBMITTED`, `APPEAL_APPROVED`, `APPEAL_DENIED`, `APPEAL_EXTENDED`) now route to the appeals channel instead of the warnings log channel.
    - Removed name-based channel lookups (`"appeal" in channel.name`) from appeal log sends; all sends resolve through the configured channel only.

### Added
- **Appeals System**:
    - Added a safety guard (`_guard_appeals_channel`) applied to every appeal send path that logs a prominent warning and blocks the send if appeal content ever targets a channel other than the configured appeals channel.
    - Accepting an appeal whose timeout already expired (or whose member left the server) now blocks the accept, marks the appeal as auto-resolved, disables the review buttons with a clear note and logs `APPEAL_AUTORESOLVED` to the appeals channel, instead of approving a punishment that no longer exists or erroring with "Member Not Found".
- **Embed Builder**:
    - `/embed` is now an interactive Components V2 builder: an ephemeral dashboard where every section (title, description, color, footer, pre-message, author, media, webhook, link button, target channel) has an Edit button that opens a modal for that section, plus Save & Cancel.
    - Title is no longer required (description stays required).
    - New options: author via user ID (name + avatar render automatically), webhook name and avatar URL for the send identity, image URL, thumbnail URL, target channel picker, and a bottom link button (label + URL, opens external links).
    - `/editembed` opens the same builder pre-filled with the existing embed's values and saves changes in place.
- **Help Menu**:
    - The `/help` and `?help` menus now render with Components V2 (containers, text displays, sections) instead of classic embeds. Category pages group commands into Slash/Hybrid/Prefix sections that fit on one message for virtually every category (pagination only kicks in above 30 commands), the home page shows a bot-avatar thumbnail, and command detail is a proper card. The category dropdown and Home/◀/▶ buttons keep working.
- **`?ls` listing commands**:
    - All `ls` outputs (`ls`, `ls role`, `ls members`, `ls perm`, `ls noperms`, `ls perms`, `ls channels`, `ls categories`, `ls bots`, `ls boosters`) now render as Components V2 containers instead of embeds. Long lists are chunked across TextDisplays in a single message, so the old 4000-char truncation hacks ("…more channels omitted", "Continued..." follow-up messages) are gone, `ls role` shows its full permission list, and `ls channels` gets a proper container per category.
- **`?appeals` list command**:
    - The admin appeal list now renders as a Components V2 dashboard with one Section per appeal (colored status badge 🟡 pending / 🟢 approved / 🔴 denied / ⚪ auto-resolved plus the user's avatar thumbnail). Up to 10 appeals per page with ◀/▶ navigation instead of cramming 20 appeals into embed fields with 100-char reasons.
- **Moderation log cards**:
    - Ban, unban, kick, timeout/mute and warn log entries now render as Components V2 cards with the user's avatar as a Section accessory (accent colors per event: red ban, green unban, orange kick, yellow timeout, gray warn) instead of classic embed fields. Everything else still falls back to classic embeds.

## [2026-01-15]

### Removed
- **Automated Moderation**:
    - Completely removed the `/automod` and `/automodstatus` commands.
    - Removed `automod_settings` configuration and event listeners from `advanced_moderation.py`.
- **Statistics**:
    - Removed the `/advmodstats` command.

### Changed
- **Diagnostics**:
    - Converted `/diag` to be a prefix-only command (`?diag`) and removed its slash command support.
- **Configuration**:
    - Fixed a crash issue in `SAMConfig` by providing a default database URI.

## [2026-01-09]

### Removed
- **Staff Shifts System**:
    - Completely removed staff shift tracking functionality (`staff_shifts.py`, `staff_shifts.db`).
    - Removed all database migrations and initialization logic for shift tracking.
    - Updated permission checks in `member_events.py` to use native Discord permissions (`manage_messages`) instead of shift status.

### Added
- **Webhook-Based Logging**:
    - Replaced direct channel messages with `WebhookManager` for all logging events.
    - Implemented intelligent caching and rate-limit handling for webhooks.
    - Added fallback to regular messages if webhooks fail.
- **Backup System Upgrade**:
    - Updated backup destination to active repository `TheCodeVerseHub/CodeVerse-Bot`.
    - Added "Critical Backup Failure" alerts to Discord logging channels.

### Fixed
- **Moderation System (`modcog.py`)**:
    - Fixed static analysis type errors in `kick` and `ban` commands.
    - Added `ephemeral` parameter handling to `_safe_reply` to prevent Interaction errors.
- **Bot Initialization**:
    - Fixed `AttributeError` in WebhookManager when `bot.user` is None during early startup.

## [2025-12-22]

### Added
- **Guild-Specific Logging System**:
    - Added `!setlogchannels` command to configure log channels per server.
    - Each guild can now have separate log channels for member, moderation, and ticket logs.
    - Added database table `guild_log_channels` to store per-guild configurations.
    - Logs are now completely isolated between different servers.
- **Persistent Views for Ticket Panels**:
    - Added database table `ticket_panels` to track all ticket panel messages.
    - Ticket panel buttons now use static custom_id `"persistent_ticket_create_button"`.
    - Added `_restore_persistent_views()` method to re-register views on bot startup.
    - Ticket panels now survive bot restarts, updates, and crashes.
- **Persistent Sticky Messages**:
    - Added `_load_sticky_messages()` method to pre-load all sticky messages on startup.
    - Sticky messages now work immediately after bot restart without configuration loss.
- **Utility Commands**:
    - Added `/getuserid <user>` command to quickly get Discord IDs from user mentions.
    - Response is ephemeral for privacy.

### Changed
- **Ticket Panel Design**:
    - Updated embed color from blue to professional black (`0x2B2D31`).
    - Removed all emojis from titles, descriptions, and bullet points.
    - Changed button style from green to grey for cleaner appearance.
    - Simplified text formatting for better readability.
- **Ticket Category Embeds**:
    - All category information panels now use black color scheme.
    - Removed emoji prefixes from category names and field titles.
    - Updated button labels to remove emojis ("Create This Ticket" instead of "🎫 Create This Ticket").
- **Logging Architecture**:
    - Removed hardcoded channel IDs for logs (`MEMBER_LOGS_CHANNEL`, `MOD_LOGS_CHANNEL`, `TICKET_LOGS_CHANNEL`).
    - Added `_get_log_channel_for_event()` method for guild-aware log routing.
    - Modified `_process_log_item()` to use guild-specific channels.

### Fixed
- **Cross-Guild Logging Issue**:
    - Fixed bug where logs from all guilds were sent to the same hardcoded channels.
    - Logs now correctly route to each guild's configured channels.
- **Ticket Button Persistence**:
    - Fixed "This interaction failed" errors after bot restarts.
    - Buttons now remain functional indefinitely without memory state.
- **Sticky Message Initialization**:
    - Fixed sticky messages not working immediately after bot restart.
    - All sticky configurations now loaded into cache on startup.

### Technical
- Added logging module to tickets.py for better error tracking.
- Integrated ticket panel persistence with database on creation.
- Improved view lifecycle management with `bot.add_view()` for message-specific views.
- Auto-cleanup of deleted ticket panel messages from database.

## [2025-12-14]

### Added
- **Report System**:
    - Added `/report` slash command to report messages by ID or Link.
    - Added "Report Message" context menu (Right-click -> Apps -> Report Message).
    - Reports are sent to a dedicated channel with an embed containing message details and attachments.
- **Slash Command Sync**:
    - Added automatic syncing of slash commands to authorized guilds on bot startup for faster updates.
    - Added `?sync` command (Owner only) for manual global syncing.

### Changed
- **User Info Command (`/info`)**:
    - Completely revamped to show detailed user information instead of bot stats.
    - Displays: General Info, Bot Sus Info (Warn Points), Whitelisted Status, Dangerous User status, Bot Permissions, and Account Accessories.
    - Removed "Badges" section and decorative emojis from values for a cleaner look.
- **Ticket System**:
    - Updated ticket categories to: Partnership, General Support, Role Issues, Reports, Warn Appeals, Other Issues.
    - Removed "Bug Report" and "Feature Request" categories.
    - Updated category descriptions, guidelines, and emojis.
    - Routed "Warn Appeals" to the report team role.
- **Logging System**:
    - Updated log embed colors for better visual distinction:
        - **Red (#ff0000)**: Ban, Kick, Timeout/Mute, Member Leave.
        - **Green (#00ff00)**: Unban, Unmute, Member Join.
    - Added specific handling for `UNMUTE` events.

### Fixed
- **Context Menu Registration**: Fixed `TypeError` when registering context menus inside a Cog by moving registration to `__init__`.
